From 71c087e33eaf4bcba7834793ba03bcdcce912f9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 15:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Cover the hardened behaviour with tests, and document the
 posture

Adds 67 tests across four areas. SsrfGuardTests pin the address ranges that must
never be treated as publicly routable, including the IPv6, IPv4-mapped, and
carrier-grade NAT cases the previous hostname blocklist missed, plus boundary
addresses either side of each private range. TenantIsolationTests prove at the
storage layer that a session id or workspace path belonging to one tenant is
invisible, undownloadable, and undeletable from another, across all three memory
backends. ProductionLockdownTests boot the host the way the shipped container
runs it and assert each previously exploitable request is now refused while
health probes and inference still succeed. StreamingChatTests assert the
Server-Sent Events contract and the enum wire formats.

Two supporting corrections came out of writing them. The security posture is now
resolved from the container rather than the builder, so it reflects the final
merged configuration instead of missing sources layered on later. Enum reading
uses LenientEnumConverter, which accepts strings and numbers but still writes
numbers, so requests in the documented string form are fixed without changing
the response format any existing client already parses.

README now describes the three postures, classifies every endpoint as public,
inference, tenant data, or administrative, lists the Security keys, and documents
the streaming event contract.
