+## Security model
+
+Auricrux resolves one security posture at startup and logs it on the first lines of the log.
+
+| Posture | When it applies | Behaviour |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Open mode** | Not Production and `Auth:Enabled` is false | All callers share the `public` tenant; administrative operations are unguarded. Local development and tests only. |
+| **Authenticated** | `Auth:Enabled` is true with an `Auth:Authority` | Callers are identified from a validated token; each gets an isolated tenant partition. |
+| **Production lockdown** | Production with no authentication configured | Account, memory, and workspace endpoints return `403` with remediation text. Health and stateless inference keep working. |
+
+Set `Security:AllowInsecureProduction=true` to knowingly serve data anonymously in Production; the
+host logs a critical warning on every boot while it is on.
+
+### Endpoint classes
+
+- **Public** — `/api/health`, `/healthz`, `/api/capabilities`, `/api/models`, `/api/account/plans`.
+- **Inference** — `/api/chat`, `/api/chat/stream`, `/api/thinking`, `/api/search`, `/api/browse`,
+  `/api/agent`, `/api/calc`, `/api/vision`. Open by default; set
+  `Security:RequireAuthForInference=true` to require a token.
+- **Tenant data** — `/api/memory/*`, `/api/workspace/*`, `/api/account/{email}`. Scoped to the
+  calling tenant. A session id or file path from another tenant resolves to a different partition
+  and is simply absent.
+- **Administrative** — `/api/account/{email}/upgrade`. Requires a constant-time match on
+  `X-Auricrux-Admin-Key`, or an authenticated principal holding the `Security:AdminRole` claim or
+  listed in `Security:AdminEmails`. Plan changes are the entitlement grant paid billing depends on,
+  so they are never self-serve.
+
+### Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Security:OpenMode` | inferred | Force shared-tenant mode on or off. |
+| `Security:AllowInsecureProduction` | `false` | Permit anonymous data access in Production. |
+| `Security:RequireAuthForInference` | `false` | Require a token for chat and other inference. |
+| `Security:AdminApiKey` | unset | Shared secret for administrative calls. Supply via environment or a secret store. |
+| `Security:AdminRole` | `auricrux-admin` | Role claim granting administrative access. |
+| `Security:MaxPromptChars` | `32000` | Largest accepted prompt. |
+| `Security:MaxUploadBytes` | `26214400` | Largest accepted workspace upload. |
+| `Security:AllowedUploadExtensions` | document/image/CAD set | Upload allow-list. |
+| `Security:Browse:AllowedPrivateHosts` | empty | Intranet hosts the SSRF guard may fetch. |
+
+### Outbound fetch safety
+
+`/api/browse` resolves the target host and refuses unless every resolved address is publicly
+routable, covering IPv6, IPv4-mapped IPv6, RFC1918, carrier-grade NAT, and link-local metadata
+ranges. Redirects are followed manually so each hop is revalidated. A hostname alone is never
+trusted, because any DNS name can be pointed at a private address.
+
+### Operator checklist
+
+1. Serve over HTTPS and keep `UseHsts` enabled.
+2. Configure `Auth:Enabled`, `Auth:Authority`, and `Auth:ClientId` before exposing the app.
+3. Set `Security:AdminApiKey` from a secret store, never from `appsettings.json`.
+4. Narrow `Cors:AllowedOrigins` to the origins you actually serve.
+5. Confirm the startup log does not report open mode or insecure production.
 
